Dear Mr. Kang,

The main problem is that this container was released from MYPKG to KRPUS inbound BKG and we want Oneway off-hire to save EQ repositioning cost.
PKGBBO did release as an I/B shipment for normal operation, so there's no reason to consider this cargo as an T/S cargo from this moment.

I'd like to give 2 options for your request.

1. Devaning cargoes at KRPUS under Shipper's account - this is because shipper and sales team only consider it as a T/S cargo. HJS operation side didn't do any wrong for this oneway operation. We released as Oneway unit & we will off-hire as an oneway at KRPUS, there's no dispute for this issue.

2. Proceed to JEA O/B loading, but all the evacuation cost from JEA to KRPUS for an 2nd off-hire should be Sipper's account. Jebel Ali is a surplus EQ area so we evacuate our EQ as HJS account. If we proceed this business, we should bare the EQ reposition cost from AEJEA to KRPUS, and who will responsible for this move?
As I explained above, no reponsibility in MYPKG, KRPUS, COE.

THKS.


